      },
      {
        "id": "E3",
        "kind": "body",
        "text": "Many DevOps teams know the incident triage pattern: An alert fires, and before anyone can fix the problem, an engineer spends 45–60 minutes figuring out what happened.",
        "sourceUrl": "https://aws.amazon.com/blogs/machine-learning/how-circle-k-accelerated-devops-incident-triage-to-under-15-minutes-with-amazon-bedrock/",
        "source": "AWS Machine Learning Blog",
        "publishedAt": "2026-11-02T17:00:58.000Z",
        "checkedAt": "2026-11-02T20:19:35.696Z"
      },
      {
        "id": "E4",
        "kind": "body",
        "text": "To address it, Circle K built an automated triage system using Amazon Bedrock , a fully managed service that makes foundation models (FMs) available through a single API.",
        "sourceUrl": "https://aws.amazon.com/blogs/machine-learning/how-circle-k-accelerated-devops-incident-triage-to-under-15-minutes-with-amazon-bedrock/",
        "source": "AWS Machine Learning Blog",
        "publishedAt": "2026-11-02T17:00:58.000Z",
        "checkedAt": "2026-11-02T20:19:35.696Z"
      },
      {
        "id": "E5",
        "kind": "body",
        "text": "Since deploying this system, Circle K has reduced mean triage time to under 15 minutes, a 67–75 percent reduction based on the team’s internal incident-response metrics.",
        "sourceUrl": "https://aws.amazon.com/blogs/machine-learning/how-circle-k-accelerated-devops-incident-triage-to-under-15-minutes-with-amazon-bedrock/",
        "source": "AWS Machine Learning Blog",
        "publishedAt": "2026-11-02T17:00:58.000Z",
        "checkedAt": "2026-11-02T20:19:35.696Z"
      },
      {
        "id": "E6",
        "kind": "body",
        "text": "When an alert came in, the triage involved a familiar sequence of manual steps: reviewing recent logs in Amazon CloudWatch , examining application-level traces in Amazon OpenSearch Service , checking Amazon Elastic Container Service (Amazon ECS) task status, and cross-referenc…",
        "sourceUrl": "https://aws.amazon.com/blogs/machine-learning/how-circle-k-accelerated-devops-incident-triage-to-under-15-minutes-with-amazon-bedrock/",
        "source": "AWS Machine Learning Blog",
        "publishedAt": "2026-11-02T17:00:58.000Z",
        "checkedAt": "2026-11-02T20:19:35.696Z"
      },
      {
        "id": "E7",
        "kind": "body",
        "text": "Because Circle K already ran on AWS, Amazon Bedrock fit into existing AWS Identity and Access Management (IAM) policies, Amazon Virtual Private Cloud (Amazon VPC) configurations, and logging pipelines.",
        "sourceUrl": "https://aws.amazon.com/blogs/machine-learning/how-circle-k-accelerated-devops-incident-triage-to-under-15-minutes-with-amazon-bedrock/",
        "source": "AWS Machine Learning Blog",
        "publishedAt": "2026-11-02T17:00:58.000Z",
        "checkedAt": "2026-11-02T20:19:35.696Z"
      },
      {
        "id": "E8",
        "kind": "body",
        "text": "Figure 1: Circle K automated incident triage architecture using Amazon Bedrock Flows",
        "sourceUrl": "https://aws.amazon.com/blogs/machine-learning/how-circle-k-accelerated-devops-incident-triage-to-under-15-minutes-with-amazon-bedrock/",
        "source": "AWS Machine Learning Blog",
        "publishedAt": "2026-11-02T17:00:58.000Z",
        "checkedAt": "2026-11-02T20:19:35.696Z"
      },
      {
        "id": "E9",
        "kind": "body",
        "text": "The Amazon Bedrock Flows architecture worked well for months, and simple incidents were triaged in under 10 minutes.",
        "sourceUrl": "https://aws.amazon.com/blogs/machine-learning/how-circle-k-accelerated-devops-incident-triage-to-under-15-minutes-with-amazon-bedrock/",
        "source": "AWS Machine Learning Blog",
        "publishedAt": "2026-11-02T17:00:58.000Z",
        "checkedAt": "2026-11-02T20:19:35.696Z"
      },
      {
        "id": "E10",
        "kind": "body",
        "text": "Amazon Bedrock AgentCore Gateway, a capability of Amazon Bedrock AgentCore, brokers the agent’s access to its data sources, including Amazon OpenSearch Service, Amazon Bedrock Knowledge Bases, and GitHub.",
        "sourceUrl": "https://aws.amazon.com/blogs/machine-learning/how-circle-k-accelerated-devops-incident-triage-to-under-15-minutes-with-amazon-bedrock/",
        "source": "AWS Machine Learning Blog",
        "publishedAt": "2026-11-02T17:00:58.000Z",
